 data to build a single view of the customer in a way that protects consumer privacy. The company's platform supports various people-based marketing solutions, including data collaboration, activation, measurement and analytics, identity, and data marketplace. It sells its solutions to enterprise marketers, agencies, marketing technology providers, publishers, and data providers in various industry verticals, such as financial, insurance and investment services, retail, automotive, telecommunications, technology, consumer packaged goods, media, healthcare, travel and hospitality, entertainment, and non-profit. The company was formerly known as Acxiom Holdings, Inc. and changed its name to LiveRamp Holdings, Inc. in October 2018. LiveRamp Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Scott E. Howe | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $625K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $128K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $64K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["LiveRamp Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.3B market cap on $813M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 0% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 67% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $166M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 8.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 4.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9920682133650597},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (39% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (35% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"